=== step 1: a bare clone ===
  configure.py
  Dockerfile
  Dockerfile.firefox
  firefox-entrypoint.sh
  justfile
  LICENSE
  podman-compose.test.yml
  podman-compose.yml
  README.md
  test
  verify.sh
  vpn_entrypoint.sh

=== step 2: just up refuses ===
The credentials are missing, or one of them is a directory.
That happens when the stack is started before ./configure.py has made them.
Run 'just configure' first.

=== step 3: configure.py creates everything ===
  The browser's VNC password was not set, so one was generated: 3wwDd6Mb18C4fwV6vhTO
  The browser's view-only VNC password was not set, so one was generated: jKNEABVFLcT3VY2wWLA4
  The warpgate admin password is not set yet.
  written to /tmp/opencode/clone3/secrets/admin_password
Warpgate
  the image runs as uid 1000
  preparing warpgate's state, this takes a moment...
  data/warpgate.yaml now points at 127.0.0.1:8443

Done. The stack is configured.

  bastion web    https://127.0.0.1:8443
  bastion ssh    ssh -p 2222 <user>@127.0.0.1
  browser vnc    127.0.0.1:6901
  admin password in /tmp/opencode/clone3/secrets/admin_password

Start it with:
  podman-compose up -d
